00:25:54.065 --> 00:25:55.081
that you can use

00:25:55.081 --> 00:25:58.303
to back up everything
you say with evidence.

00:25:58.303 --> 00:26:01.110
This is part four in a five part series

00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:02.784
on how to speak clearly and confidently.

00:26:02.784 --> 00:26:04.920
I'll put links to the entire series

00:26:04.920 --> 00:26:07.560
below once all five parts are posted.

00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:10.620
Let's now learn to use
the PREP talking points.

00:26:10.620 --> 00:26:13.620
PREP is an acronym which you
probably know I don't like,

00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:15.300
so let me quickly explain this.

00:26:15.300 --> 00:26:17.070
When you have something important to say,

00:26:17.070 --> 00:26:18.420
do it in this order.

00:26:18.420 --> 00:26:20.010
State your point of view.

00:26:20.010 --> 00:26:22.440
Next, give a reason for your point of view

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:25.050
and then you give a concrete example

00:26:25.050 --> 00:26:28.650
or other evidence that
illustrates your point of view.

00:26:28.650 --> 00:26:30.990
When you add even a little
bit of evidence like this,

00:26:30.990 --> 00:26:33.876
you'll sound much more
confident and persuasive.

00:26:33.876 --> 00:26:37.020
And then you restate your
point of view at the end

00:26:37.020 --> 00:26:39.120
to show that you've
finished your talking turn.

00:26:39.120 --> 00:26:43.230
I consider the second P in
the PREP method optional,

00:26:43.230 --> 00:26:46.770
depending upon the situation
and the length of your message.

00:26:46.770 --> 00:26:48.780
We'll talk through some
examples in a moment,

00:26:48.780 --> 00:26:50.190
but first, the PREP method

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:51.960
and talking points comes from the world

00:26:51.960 --> 00:26:53.520
of impromptu speaking.

00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:56.520
In the real world, the
PREP points are useful

00:26:56.520 --> 00:26:58.980
for any kind of group meeting situation,

00:26:58.980 --> 00:27:02.820
high stakes conversation
or during a Q&amp;A session

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:05.100
where you have two simultaneous goals.

00:27:05.100 --> 00:27:08.130
First, you wanna sound clear
and concise and confident,

00:27:08.130 --> 00:27:10.140
but second, you also wanna make sure

00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:12.681
you support what you say with evidence

00:27:12.681 --> 00:27:15.270
and stay on track while you do it.

00:27:15.270 --> 00:27:17.820
You can use this for a
message that's as short

00:27:17.820 --> 00:27:21.780
as three sentences or
let's say 15 to 20 seconds,

00:27:21.780 --> 00:27:26.780
or you can develop it a bit
into a 30 to 45 second message.

00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:28.050
Let's walk through this.

00:27:28.050 --> 00:27:31.170
Here are the first two
examples of how I would sound

00:27:31.170 --> 00:27:32.970
in an everyday conversation.

00:27:32.970 --> 00:27:34.380
For these first two examples,

00:27:34.380 --> 00:27:37.650
we'll do the short version
of about 15 seconds or so

00:27:37.650 --> 00:27:40.233
and I'll leave off the
optional P at the end

00:27:40.233 --> 00:27:44.310
because it's really not necessary
for a message this short.

00:27:44.310 --> 00:27:45.810
Here's my first example:

00:27:45.810 --> 00:27:48.900
Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:51.390
and I think we should get on board.

00:27:51.390 --> 00:27:53.310
One reason for its popularity

00:27:53.310 --> 00:27:56.130
is that anybody at any
skill level can play.

00:27:56.130 --> 00:27:58.860
For example, I have a
friend who is 80 years old

00:27:58.860 --> 00:28:00.930
and plays couples with her husband,

00:28:00.930 --> 00:28:04.320
but when her grandchildren
visit, they all play together.

00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:06.810
Here's another example of
what that would sound like

00:28:06.810 --> 00:28:08.610
in a professional situation.

00:28:08.610 --> 00:28:11.760
We'll pretend we're in a
group meeting with your team

00:28:11.760 --> 00:28:13.980
and we're talking about
what vendor your team

00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:15.750
should work with moving forward.

00:28:15.750 --> 00:28:18.523
It's now your turn to voice your opinion

00:28:18.523 --> 00:28:20.597
and you're going to use the PRE points.

00:28:21.450 --> 00:28:23.137
For example, you could say,

00:28:23.137 --> 00:28:25.230
"I recommend we hire vendor A

00:28:25.230 --> 00:28:27.690
because we already know
they do quality work

00:28:27.690 --> 00:28:29.670
and they're easy to work with.

00:28:29.670 --> 00:28:32.130
Our last project with them, for example,

00:28:32.130 --> 00:28:35.640
came in under budget and a
month ahead of schedule."

00:28:35.640 --> 00:28:38.340
In mere seconds, you
can use the PREP method

00:28:38.340 --> 00:28:41.100
to express yourself
clearly and confidently

00:28:41.100 --> 00:28:44.700
and back up what you say
with a concrete example.

00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:46.680
Let's do some additional fine-tuning

00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:49.500
so we can really
understand each point here

00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:51.450
and that will also help us expand this

00:28:51.450 --> 00:28:54.270
to a 30 or 45-second message.

00:28:54.270 --> 00:28:56.220
The first P is pretty straightforward.

00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:58.740
This is where you express
your point of view,

00:28:58.740 --> 00:29:01.500
position, or opinion about a subject.

00:29:01.500 --> 00:29:03.870
This is your bottom line.

00:29:03.870 --> 00:29:06.690
In school, you might call
this your thesis statement.

00:29:06.690 --> 00:29:08.400
My tip for the P is that

00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:09.750
this is what you would say

00:29:09.750 --> 00:29:11.790
if you were only allowed to say

00:29:11.790 --> 00:29:15.090
what you thought in one concise sentence.

00:29:15.090 --> 00:29:17.176
Next, the R stands for reason.

00:29:17.176 --> 00:29:20.040
This is where you will
give a clear explanation

00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:24.150
of why you have that point
of view in the first place.

00:29:24.150 --> 00:29:25.500
This answers a question

00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:27.892
listeners will usually ask themselves

00:29:27.892 --> 00:29:29.790
before they realize it.

00:29:29.790 --> 00:29:31.140
They might be thinking for example,

00:29:31.140 --> 00:29:33.600
well, why do you believe that?

00:29:33.600 --> 00:29:36.420
To make it bulletproof,
the way I coach my clients

00:29:36.420 --> 00:29:39.549
is to literally use words like because,

00:29:39.549 --> 00:29:42.532
or start with the phrase,
"The reason is..."

00:29:42.532 --> 00:29:46.105
The reason is when you start
with those lead-in keywords,

00:29:46.105 --> 00:29:48.120
you will usually be able to
find the rest of the words

00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:50.580
to offer a clear reason
for your point of view.

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:53.760
That's exactly what I did
for my previous examples.

00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:56.190
When I talked about the
popularity of pickleball,

00:29:56.190 --> 00:29:59.490
I used the lead in phrase, "One reason."

00:29:59.490 --> 00:30:00.870
For the professional example,

00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:03.510
I said I wanted to do
business with vendor A

00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:05.845
and I signaled that I was giving a reason

00:30:05.845 --> 00:30:08.610
by using the keyword "Because."

00:30:08.610 --> 00:30:11.130
So my tip for the R, the reason,

00:30:11.130 --> 00:30:13.200
is that if you're not sure how to explain

00:30:13.200 --> 00:30:15.479
why you have that point
of view, use keywords

00:30:15.479 --> 00:30:18.690
like reason or because as
you draft your message,

00:30:18.690 --> 00:30:20.190
and that will usually help you state

00:30:20.190 --> 00:30:21.660
your reason more clearly.

00:30:21.660 --> 00:30:23.100
With that in mind, let's talk about

00:30:23.100 --> 00:30:27.420
how to turn this into a
30 to 45-second message.

00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:29.790
For a slightly longer message like this,

00:30:29.790 --> 00:30:34.290
the first two steps, the P and
the R stay exactly the same.

00:30:34.290 --> 00:30:38.340
You should still express your
point of view in one sentence

00:30:38.340 --> 00:30:40.050
and give your reasons in one

00:30:40.050 --> 00:30:43.110
or perhaps two very concise sentences.

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:46.380
But as mentioned, the E stands
for example or evidence.

00:30:46.380 --> 00:30:50.190
In my earlier illustrations,
my examples were quite short,

00:30:50.190 --> 00:30:52.260
but a longer message usually means

00:30:52.260 --> 00:30:55.350
providing additional examples or evidence.

00:30:55.350 --> 00:30:58.050
The E is really the only talking point

00:30:58.050 --> 00:31:01.559
in prep that you can expand
without repeating yourself.

00:31:01.559 --> 00:31:03.690
And to transition to your examples,

00:31:03.690 --> 00:31:06.540
just use the lead-in
phrase, "For example,"

00:31:06.540 --> 00:31:08.760
and then immediately
share your illustration

00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:10.320
or other evidence.

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:12.720
For pickleball, I could have
added additional examples

00:31:12.720 --> 00:31:15.390
to make this into a longer message.

00:31:15.390 --> 00:31:16.950
I originally gave examples about

00:31:16.950 --> 00:31:19.144
how my 80-year-old friend plays

00:31:19.144 --> 00:31:21.720
and they also play with
their grandchildren,

00:31:21.720 --> 00:31:23.966
but let's say I was sharing this message

00:31:23.966 --> 00:31:27.570
with my local parks and
recreation department and leaders,

00:31:27.570 --> 00:31:31.170
and I wanted to convince them
to add some pickleball courts

00:31:31.170 --> 00:31:32.790
to our community center.

00:31:32.790 --> 00:31:35.750
For that audience, I would
add some other evidence

00:31:35.750 --> 00:31:38.698
in the form of statistics
and other information.

00:31:38.698 --> 00:31:39.872
I would've shared

00:31:39.872 --> 00:31:42.930
that the association for
pickleball professionals

00:31:42.930 --> 00:31:46.800
shows that over 36 million
Americans now play the sport.

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.930
It's now more popular than tennis.

00:31:48.930 --> 00:31:50.610
I would've mentioned that the cost

00:31:50.610 --> 00:31:52.740
of pickleball is less than half

00:31:52.740 --> 00:31:54.480
of what it costs to play tennis.

00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:56.790
I would've mentioned
that three nearby towns

00:31:56.790 --> 00:32:00.387
now have dedicated pickleball
courts and leagues.

00:32:00.387 --> 00:32:03.600
You'll notice that each
additional piece of information

00:32:03.600 --> 00:32:06.330
and evidence is unique and
that's really important.

00:32:06.330 --> 00:32:09.428
Make sure each example
adds new information

00:32:09.428 --> 00:32:12.030
so that you don't simply repeat yourself

00:32:12.030 --> 00:32:13.410
and get long-winded.

00:32:13.410 --> 00:32:14.490
I could do the same thing

00:32:14.490 --> 00:32:16.997
with my example about hiring vendor A.

00:32:16.997 --> 00:32:18.990
I would add additional examples

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:21.090
and evidence that back up my message

00:32:21.090 --> 00:32:22.650
without repeating myself,

00:32:22.650 --> 00:32:25.050
so to expand a prep message

00:32:25.050 --> 00:32:27.480
to between 30 and 45 seconds,

00:32:27.480 --> 00:32:29.804
the only point you expand on is the E

00:32:29.804 --> 00:32:31.800
by adding more examples and evidence.

00:32:31.800 --> 00:32:32.970
The other talking points

00:32:32.970 --> 00:32:34.470
stay exactly the same,

00:32:34.470 --> 00:32:36.240
but now because your
message is a bit longer,

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:39.690
this justifies adding
the second P to the end.

00:32:39.690 --> 00:32:42.660
This is where you restate
your point of view.

00:32:42.660 --> 00:32:44.220
The second P, if you think about it,

00:32:44.220 --> 00:32:47.190
functions as a one-sentence
mini conclusion

00:32:47.190 --> 00:32:48.029
for your message.

00:32:48.029 --> 00:32:50.550
You might reword the second
P a little differently

00:32:50.550 --> 00:32:53.160
than the first, but it must reiterate

00:32:53.160 --> 00:32:54.824
your original point of view

00:32:54.824 --> 00:32:56.910
to show that you're finished talking.

00:32:56.910 --> 00:32:59.070
I would say, "And that's why I believe

00:32:59.070 --> 00:33:01.410
we should get on board with pickleball.

00:33:01.410 --> 00:33:04.984
Or, "To me, vendor A is the right choice."

00:33:04.984 --> 00:33:07.710
To summarize, use the PRE points

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:09.455
if you have a brief message to share

00:33:09.455 --> 00:33:11.970
and want to support that with evidence.

00:33:11.970 --> 00:33:15.060
And use the entire prep
method with the second P,

00:33:15.060 --> 00:33:16.590
if you have a slightly longer message

00:33:16.590 --> 00:33:17.790
and want to support everything you say

00:33:17.790 --> 00:33:21.297
with additional examples
and more evidence.

00:33:21.297 --> 00:33:25.620
Both are extremely tight
ways to make a point

00:33:25.620 --> 00:33:27.750
and you now know how to
express yourself clearly

00:33:27.750 --> 00:33:30.570
and confidently and back
up everything you say

00:33:30.570 --> 00:33:32.520
without getting long-winded.

