group coaching options
and a variety of classes

00:34:40.380 --> 00:34:43.380
and communication, public
speaking and leadership.

00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:45.897
Today's video is all about
speaking with conviction

00:34:45.897 --> 00:34:49.500
and the bottom line is if
you have something to say,

00:34:49.500 --> 00:34:51.526
say it like you mean it.

00:34:51.526 --> 00:34:54.540
Tip number one to speak
with more conviction

00:34:54.540 --> 00:34:57.420
is to increase your volume.

00:34:57.420 --> 00:35:00.510
I would say that more than
half of the clients I work with

00:35:00.510 --> 00:35:03.480
do not speak loudly
enough in group situations

00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:05.490
or during presentations.

00:35:05.490 --> 00:35:08.040
The trouble is people who speak softly

00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:11.070
generally do not sound confident
in what they're saying.

00:35:11.070 --> 00:35:13.890
If you speak at a below average volume,

00:35:13.890 --> 00:35:17.190
it's going to create a
below average impression.

00:35:17.190 --> 00:35:19.320
In contrast, if you can
increase your volume

00:35:19.320 --> 00:35:22.410
by just 10 or 20%, everything you say

00:35:22.410 --> 00:35:25.710
will sound more
enthusiastic and committed.

00:35:25.710 --> 00:35:27.570
If you're in a one-on-one
conversation, of course,

00:35:27.570 --> 00:35:31.230
you have to keep the level
of volume conversational,

00:35:31.230 --> 00:35:33.588
but in front of a group
of almost any size,

00:35:33.588 --> 00:35:36.990
increase your volume by about 10 or 20%.

00:35:36.990 --> 00:35:37.950
For public speaking,

00:35:37.950 --> 00:35:40.920
the tip is to let your
voice fill the room.

00:35:40.920 --> 00:35:43.860
The larger the room and the
more people that are there,

00:35:43.860 --> 00:35:46.290
the more volume you use.

00:35:46.290 --> 00:35:47.570
When you speak a little louder,

00:35:47.570 --> 00:35:49.125
it'll make everything you say

00:35:49.125 --> 00:35:51.870
like you're speaking with conviction.

00:35:51.870 --> 00:35:53.790
When I work with clients,
we'll often do this

00:35:53.790 --> 00:35:55.110
in workshops with somebody

00:35:55.110 --> 00:35:57.810
who is speaking too softly for the room.

00:35:57.810 --> 00:35:59.790
They volunteer and we put them up there

00:35:59.790 --> 00:36:00.780
in front of everybody.

00:36:00.780 --> 00:36:02.020
We're really supportive

00:36:02.020 --> 00:36:05.310
and we gradually get them to speak louder.

00:36:05.310 --> 00:36:07.650
And you can try this with me right now

00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:09.810
and I'm going to use a sample sentence

00:36:09.810 --> 00:36:13.020
about pickleball from a
previous lesson in this series.

00:36:13.020 --> 00:36:15.120
We'll gradually increase the volume

00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:16.950
and it's just about pickleball,

00:36:16.950 --> 00:36:19.470
but you'll see how this
makes a difference.

00:36:19.470 --> 00:36:23.977
Repeat the sentence after me
in your normal speaking volume.

00:36:23.977 --> 00:36:28.230
"Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around."

00:36:28.230 --> 00:36:29.340
Now, let's say that again,

00:36:29.340 --> 00:36:32.580
and this time, let's speak 10% louder

00:36:32.580 --> 00:36:36.007
and let your voice start to
fill whatever room you're in.

00:36:36.007 --> 00:36:39.930
"Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around."

00:36:39.930 --> 00:36:42.090
Now let's increase the
volume one more time

00:36:42.090 --> 00:36:45.270
to 20% higher than your normal volume.

00:36:45.270 --> 00:36:46.867
And say it again with me.

00:36:46.867 --> 00:36:51.000
"Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around."

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:51.960
Now, I'm not there with you,

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:53.379
but I'm willing to speculate

00:36:53.379 --> 00:36:55.680
that when you speak a little louder,

00:36:55.680 --> 00:36:57.177
you'll sound more confident

00:36:57.177 --> 00:37:00.150
and convinced about what you just said.

00:37:00.150 --> 00:37:03.420
You may also notice as you
practice speaking louder,

00:37:03.420 --> 00:37:04.350
that you're benefiting

00:37:04.350 --> 00:37:07.050
from a few other positive side effects.

00:37:07.050 --> 00:37:08.610
I've noticed that when most

00:37:08.610 --> 00:37:10.920
of my clients increase their volume,

00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:13.177
they also increase their vocal variety

00:37:13.177 --> 00:37:14.670
in the sound of their voice,

00:37:14.670 --> 00:37:16.740
so they no longer sound monotone.

00:37:16.740 --> 00:37:19.110
That's because increasing your volume

00:37:19.110 --> 00:37:22.170
naturally improves your
tone and inflection.

00:37:22.170 --> 00:37:23.580
My clients also usually start

00:37:23.580 --> 00:37:25.530
to become more animated in terms

00:37:25.530 --> 00:37:27.480
of their gestures in their body language

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:29.010
and their facial expressions.

00:37:29.010 --> 00:37:30.930
I can't obviously see you right now,

00:37:30.930 --> 00:37:32.040
but let me ask,

00:37:32.040 --> 00:37:34.170
did you notice that
your facial expressions

00:37:34.170 --> 00:37:37.800
became more animated when
you increased your volume?

00:37:37.800 --> 00:37:41.460
Did you gesture with your
hands without realizing it?

00:37:41.460 --> 00:37:43.170
All of that will make you come across

00:37:43.170 --> 00:37:45.600
as more confident in what you're saying.

00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:48.210
So all you have to do
is increase your volume

00:37:48.210 --> 00:37:49.950
by about 10% or 20%

00:37:49.950 --> 00:37:52.470
and you'll look and sound
like you're speaking

00:37:52.470 --> 00:37:54.210
with more conviction.

00:37:54.210 --> 00:37:57.060
Tip number two, so speak
with more conviction,

00:37:57.060 --> 00:38:01.650
is to emphasize the most
important words in each sentence.

00:38:01.650 --> 00:38:03.900
In fact, I just did that
in my previous sentence,

00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:05.130
so I'll do it again

00:38:05.130 --> 00:38:08.197
and you tell me which words I emphasized.

00:38:08.197 --> 00:38:09.750
"To speak with more conviction.

00:38:09.750 --> 00:38:13.789
Emphasize the most important
words in each sentence."

00:38:13.789 --> 00:38:16.620
Did you hear it? And you can do the same.

00:38:16.620 --> 00:38:18.088
All I did was slow down

00:38:18.088 --> 00:38:20.490
and lean into what I considered

00:38:20.490 --> 00:38:22.560
to be the most important words,

00:38:22.560 --> 00:38:25.680
and you should do that
in every single sentence.

00:38:25.680 --> 00:38:28.140
Just pick whatever two or three words

00:38:28.140 --> 00:38:30.120
in a row matter the most in each sentence.

00:38:30.120 --> 00:38:33.150
Slow down and add emphasis to them.

00:38:33.150 --> 00:38:36.270
There are lots of reasons
to emphasize keywords.

00:38:36.270 --> 00:38:38.610
The first is that when
people speak too rapidly

00:38:38.610 --> 00:38:40.140
and rush through every thought

00:38:40.140 --> 00:38:42.540
and every sentence, it
doesn't sound confident.

00:38:42.540 --> 00:38:45.630
It sounds like they're just
trying to get through a message

00:38:45.630 --> 00:38:48.330
and their main goal is
to get it over with.

00:38:48.330 --> 00:38:51.480
Now, rushing through may
help you accomplish the goal

00:38:51.480 --> 00:38:53.670
of finishing as fast as possible,

00:38:53.670 --> 00:38:55.320
but it's not going to make you sound

00:38:55.320 --> 00:38:57.510
like you believe what you're saying.

00:38:57.510 --> 00:39:01.680
Another reason people rush is
because of anxiety and nerves.

00:39:01.680 --> 00:39:04.230
But whatever reason you have
for speaking too quickly,

00:39:04.230 --> 00:39:06.300
emphasizing the most important words

00:39:06.300 --> 00:39:08.430
in each and every sentence

00:39:08.430 --> 00:39:11.490
will give you a much more
confident-sounding rhythm.

00:39:11.490 --> 00:39:12.630
It also helps your listeners

00:39:12.630 --> 00:39:15.090
because now they know
that if it's important

00:39:15.090 --> 00:39:16.906
to you as a speaker, then you're signaling

00:39:16.906 --> 00:39:19.200
that it should be important to them.

00:39:19.200 --> 00:39:21.240
And here's another tip within a tip.

00:39:21.240 --> 00:39:23.640
When you get to the end
of your talking turn,

00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:26.430
make sure you use the
same type of emphasis

00:39:26.430 --> 00:39:29.400
on the last three words you say.

00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:32.327
And make sure your voice
goes down at the end

00:39:32.327 --> 00:39:35.250
toward the period punctuation mark.

00:39:35.250 --> 00:39:37.680
It should sound like you
are landing the plane

00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:39.150
on your talking turn.

00:39:39.150 --> 00:39:41.160
Let's use our pickleball example again

00:39:41.160 --> 00:39:42.570
and say it along with me.

00:39:42.570 --> 00:39:45.660
We'll pretend that this is
the end of our talking turn.

00:39:45.660 --> 00:39:47.370
Emphasize the last three words

00:39:47.370 --> 00:39:50.887
as you read this and notice
how certain you sound.

00:39:50.887 --> 00:39:55.230
"Pickleball is now one of the
most popular sports around."

00:39:55.230 --> 00:39:57.360
You really wanna lean into
those last three words.

00:39:57.360 --> 00:40:00.120
Make sure it sounds like
you're making a statement

00:40:00.120 --> 00:40:01.887
and not asking a question.

00:40:01.887 --> 00:40:04.470
Third, let's talk about eye contact

00:40:04.470 --> 00:40:06.990
and how you can use this to come across

00:40:06.990 --> 00:40:07.950
as more confident,

00:40:07.950 --> 00:40:10.680
like you really believe
what you just said.

00:40:10.680 --> 00:40:11.790
Before I give you this tip,

00:40:11.790 --> 00:40:14.310
let me explain how I learned this myself.

00:40:14.310 --> 00:40:16.080
I've been going to group meetings

00:40:16.080 --> 00:40:19.260
as a participant and coaching
clients for decades now.

00:40:19.260 --> 00:40:21.870
And I've noticed a very subtle behavior

00:40:21.870 --> 00:40:24.570
that differentiates the
most confident speakers

00:40:24.570 --> 00:40:26.610
from everybody else in the room.

00:40:26.610 --> 00:40:29.010
First and most obviously,
confident speakers

00:40:29.010 --> 00:40:30.470
tend to make direct eye contact

00:40:30.470 --> 00:40:32.520
with people as they're speaking.

00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:34.778
That's probably not too surprising,

00:40:34.778 --> 00:40:37.230
and I would guess, like most people,

00:40:37.230 --> 00:40:39.930
you make at least some direct eye contact

00:40:39.930 --> 00:40:41.790
when you're speaking, but if you don't,

00:40:41.790 --> 00:40:43.872
make sure you practice eye contact

00:40:43.872 --> 00:40:46.470
while you're speaking
and sharing your message.

00:40:46.470 --> 00:40:49.140
A second: Here's the
subtle difference I noticed

00:40:49.140 --> 00:40:50.550
about eye contact.

00:40:50.550 --> 00:40:53.880
When the most confident speakers
finish their talking turns,

00:40:53.880 --> 00:40:57.210
they keep their eyes and their chin up

00:40:57.210 --> 00:40:59.171
and they continue to make eye contact

00:40:59.171 --> 00:41:02.490
with the next person in
the group who speaks.

00:41:02.490 --> 00:41:05.850
They don't stare or
glare at the next person

00:41:05.850 --> 00:41:07.140
in a confrontational way.

00:41:07.140 --> 00:41:09.330
They simply maintain eye contact

00:41:09.330 --> 00:41:11.310
with whoever speaks next.

00:41:11.310 --> 00:41:14.910
In contrast, professionals
who seem to lack confidence

00:41:14.910 --> 00:41:17.640
in what they said, finish
their talking turn,

00:41:17.640 --> 00:41:19.170
and then they drop their eyes

00:41:19.170 --> 00:41:21.870
and their chin toward the
table, toward their notes

00:41:21.870 --> 00:41:23.250
or toward a device.

00:41:23.250 --> 00:41:25.110
And when they break eye contact like that

00:41:25.110 --> 00:41:26.880
and look down after they speak,

00:41:26.880 --> 00:41:29.231
it creates the impression
that they don't believe in

00:41:29.231 --> 00:41:32.460
or stand behind what they just said.

00:41:32.460 --> 00:41:35.370
To reiterate the tip, when
you finish your talking turn

00:41:35.370 --> 00:41:38.400
in a group situation, keep your chin up,

00:41:38.400 --> 00:41:41.730
maintain eye contact
with whoever speaks next,

00:41:41.730 --> 00:41:43.954
and it will cast a very positive light

00:41:43.954 --> 00:41:45.730
on what you just said,

00:41:45.730 --> 00:41:49.410
and it'll come across like
you stand behind your message.

00:41:49.410 --> 00:41:52.260
If you watched all five
videos in this series

00:41:52.260 --> 00:41:54.330
on how to speak clearly and confidently,

00:41:54.330 --> 00:41:55.687
please let me know in a comment.

00:41:55.687 --> 00:41:59.250
I would love to celebrate that
with you with my own comment,

00:41:59.250 --> 00:42:00.990
and I will give you a heart.

00:42:00.990 --> 00:42:03.210
And don't forget to take
a look at my website.

00:42:03.210 --> 00:42:06.240
There's free resources
there that I mentioned,

00:42:06.240 --> 00:42:09.120
group coaching options and classes.

00:42:09.120 --> 00:42:11.160
Thank you for joining me in this journey.

00:42:11.160 --> 00:42:14.160
Until next time, thanks, God
bless, and I will see you soon.

